==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|maddoc}}, from an unrecorded {{etyl|ang|en}} form corresponding to Old Norse {{m|non|maðkr}} (whence dialectal English {{m|en|mawk}}, Danish {{m|da|madike}}, Swedish {{m|sv|mask}}), originally a diminutive of the {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*maþô||worm}} (whence Old English {{m|ang|maþa}}), equivalent to {{suffix|made|t1=maggot|ock|lang=en}}.

